WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.620
In 1948, the historian Arthur Schlesinger

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.870
asked fellow historians to rate US

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:11.910
presidents. The pollsters soon followed suit,

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:13.590
and they've been asking Americans to

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:15.929
assess presidents ever since. Barack Obama

00:00:15.929 --> 00:00:17.670
leaves office with a solid approval

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:20.460
rating. He's in the mid-fifties in most polls,

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.289
but when it comes to job performance, the

00:00:22.289 --> 00:00:24.150
verdict is mixed. President Obama

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.279
inherited a terrible economy. Although

00:00:26.279 --> 00:00:27.990
Americans see some improvement after

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.390
eight years, only a bare majority approve of

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:32.009
the job he's doing here.

00:00:32.009 --> 00:00:33.510
Less than half approve of the job he's

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:35.820
doing handling terrorism or foreign policy

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.340
generally. Sixty-one percent believe that the US

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.780
is less respected that in the past.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:42.420
As for Obamacare, views about the law have

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:43.770
generally been more negative than

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:45.899
positive since its passage. A solid

00:00:45.899 --> 00:00:47.340
majority disapprove of the way the

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.020
president has handled the issue. However,

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.149
only thirty-five percent favor straight

00:00:51.149 --> 00:00:53.309
repeal. Finally, two-thirds in a pew survey say

00:00:53.309 --> 00:00:55.260
race relations have gotten worse since

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:59.520
2008. Only nine percent say they've gotten better. First

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:01.440
drafts of history are always subject to

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.080
revision. At this point, we know that

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.570
President Obama is personally more popular

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:10.290
than his policies. To learn more about my take on

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:12.479
Obama's legacy, check the links in the

00:01:12.479 --> 00:01:14.760
description below. Also, let us know what

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:16.650
other topics you'd like AEI scholars to

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:19.000
cover in 60 seconds.

